	Well, the response to my post has been more favorable than I 
ever expected.  Here are some more ideas and some follow-ups.

	The henchman idea has taken a little different turn than I had
in mind, but what the hell...this is what I thought:

	The henchman should be more like an Igor figure.  He(she) would
lug around goods for you.  If he/she came upon some treasure of some kind
he/she would pick it up.  He/she might sell it to you if you did not give 
it to him/her, and if he did sell it to you, it should be at a big 
discount over the shop prices.  He/she would pick up stuff in a store,
but would not necessarily know what was cursed.  The store stuff he
would sell you.
	As far as mapping and the like, I think it should work like this:
when you and Igor go down the steps to a new level, he should begin to
wander on his own.  When you and he/she meet up again, you would chat 
and he/she would tell you the things that he has found.  This would
include items, rooms, traps and a part of the map that he has 
travelled.  Maybe you could pay him/her extra for helping you fight
against a monster, this would be on a pay-per-fight basis.  If you could
aquire a few henchman, and they became unhappy with the way you run things,
a mutiny would breakout, and they would try to take over.  These are just
a few suggestions, feel free to add you own here...


	As far as the mirror issue goes, I kinda like it.  The idea of
walking through a mirror into a parallel universe is kinda intriging.  Would
this be only for the current level?  How about a level portal?  Walk 
through on level 5 and poof...level 25.  You could walk back and forth 
between the two levels.  Or how about:

	You look into the mirror, -More-
	an endless stream of Medusae pour out of the mirror...

better have a blindfold handy...


	While on the subject of blinfolds, I think that if you are
telepathic, you should be able to cover you eyes with your hands.  You 
would have to wield nothing, and it would only last for one turn.  Maybe if
you were wearing a cursed pair of gloves, they might stick to your face.
Bummer.

	I did not see much response to the dungeon level issues.  I just
finished a game when the amulet was on level 50 and seeing 20 levels
of plain old mazes got to be a little boring.  This is what I would like
to see:  how about a random room within the maze.  Not a special level
like the stronghold or the towers, but just a room here and there.  I like
the mall idea, the wandering guard(s) should be a fair enemy, not the weenie
keystone kops.  How about this:  A treasure level (level 15 or greater)
where you walk down the steps and you begin on one side of the level.  The
level would be basically linear in the sense that one room would lead to
another. (that is there would be no situations where room A leads to room B
and B to C, and C to A.)  In the last couple of rooms, there would be a 
boatload of monsters, and maybe a part of a maze.  Once you get to the end 
of the rooms, there would be some mirrors on the wall.  If you pick the
right one, it would teleport you to the treasure level.  On this level,
there would be no stairs, many traps(nothing to take you off the level),
there could be an army barracks, a beehive, a zoo and just a whole bunch
of bad guys.  At the end of this, there would be a room full of treasure.
This could be the ancient dragon room that was discussed a while back.
Of course you would have to figure out how to get back to the original 
level that you were on, and the guardians of the treasure would do their
best to stop you, but...

	Essentially, we need more creativity in the dungeon creating
department. How about some non-rectangular rooms?  Something...throw me 
a bone someone....


	Oh well, enuf of my longwindedness.  OK hacksters, sink your 
teeth into this one.

